; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Countdown to Liftoff
; CATEGORY: Recursion
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, debugger, call stack, stop rule
; SUMMARY:  A procedure that counts down by calling itself with a smaller number, drawing a rocket at liftoff.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   COUNTDOWN prints 10, 9, 8 ... 1 and then "Liftoff!". It never uses
;   REPEAT or FOR. Instead it prints one number and asks a fresh copy of
;   itself to count down from one less. When the number reaches 0 the
;   last copy draws a rocket and stops.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   1. Press Run once and read the printout.
;   2. Click in the margin next to the line  print :n  inside COUNTDOWN.
;      A red dot appears.
;   3. Press Run (F5). The program stops before printing 10.
;      Open the Variables panel: :n is 10.
;   4. Press F5 again. Now :n is 9. Open the Call Stack panel: there are
;      TWO countdowns listed. The first one has not finished; it is waiting
;      for the second one. Keep pressing F5 and watch the stack grow.
;   5. Click an older line in the Call Stack. Its own :n is still there,
;      untouched. Every copy of the procedure keeps its own :n.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a procedure that calls itself (recursion)
;   * the stop rule (base case) that ends the chain
;   * every call has its own private copy of its inputs
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change countdown 10 to countdown 3 or countdown 25.
;   * Delete the stop rule line and run it. What goes wrong? (Press Stop.)
;   * Make it count down by 2. Which stop rule do you need now?
; ============================================================

; The stop rule comes FIRST. If it were after the recursive call,
; the procedure would call itself forever before ever checking.
to countdown :n
  if :n = 0 [liftoff stop]
  print :n
  ; a short pause so you can feel the count
  wait 15
  countdown :n - 1
end

; Draws a little rocket with a flame, then flies it upward.
to liftoff
  print "Liftoff!
  penup setxy 0 -200 setheading 0 pendown
  rocket
  repeat 30 [
    clean
    penup fd 12 pendown
    rocket
    wait 2
  ]
end

; The rocket is drawn from its bottom middle and returns there, facing
; up again, so it can be redrawn anywhere just by moving the turtle first.
to rocket
  ; the body: up the left side, a pointed nose, down the right side
  setpencolor 15
  filled 15 [lt 90 fd 15 rt 90 fd 70 rt 30 fd 30 rt 120 fd 30 rt 30 fd 70 rt 90 fd 15 rt 90]
  ; The window is drawn AFTER the body. Later drawing covers earlier
  ; drawing, so the thing that should end up on top has to come last.
  penup fd 38 pendown
  setpencolor 11
  filled 11 [rt 45 repeat 4 [fd 10 lt 90] lt 45]
  penup bk 38 pendown
  ; the flame hangs below the body
  setpencolor 14
  filled 14 [rt 90 fd 10 rt 111.8 fd 26.9 rt 136.4 fd 26.9 rt 111.8 fd 10 lt 90]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [10 10 40]
countdown 10
